What is a Pedestal Paver System?
Pedestal Paver Systems are height-adjustable support structures used in construction, renovation, and landscaping projects. These systems consist of load-bearing plates, adjustable bases, and connecting mechanisms that enable precise leveling on uneven surfaces. Widely adopted for decks, terraces, and rooftop gardens, they offer superior drainage, waterproofing, and durability compared to traditional installation methods.
With modular design and material innovations, these systems have become the preferred choice for architects and contractors seeking efficient, long-lasting solutions for elevated outdoor spaces. Their ability to accommodate various paving materials while maintaining structural integrity continues to revolutionize urban landscape architecture.
